SCOPE

maniMon is a system monitoring tool. It contains no part of, and
discloses nothing about, the photonic-ternary hardware or software
covered by the author's patent applications. It is published
separately and independently of those works.

----------------------------------------------------------------------

HARDWARE INTERFACE NOTES

The amdgpu gpu_metrics v1_3 structure layout in health.py was
determined empirically from live sysfs output on a Radeon Pro W7900
(RDNA 3, gfx1100), cross-checked field by field against independent
hwmon readings. The throttler bit assignments follow the Linux kernel
enum smu_throttler. Neither is a redistribution of kernel source.

SMART attribute interpretations follow the conventions documented by
the smartmontools project. Where a vendor's use of an attribute is
ambiguous, maniMon publishes the raw counter rather than guessing —
see README.md, "Honesty about units".

----------------------------------------------------------------------

THIRD-PARTY TOOLS INVOKED AT RUNTIME

maniMon executes the following programs when present. None is bundled,
modified, or redistributed; each remains under its own licence:

  ipmitool      BSD          BMC sensor readings
  smartmontools GPL-2.0+     SATA and SAS SMART
  nvme-cli      GPL-2.0+     NVMe SMART
  dmidecode     GPL-2.0+     DIMM inventory
  git           GPL-2.0      repository status
  systemctl     LGPL-2.1+    service status

Python dependencies are the standard library plus PyGObject (LGPL-2.1+)
for the GTK panels. The non-graphical components — collectors, sensors,
metric store and run accounting — require no third-party Python packages.
